{
  "summary": "Peer review and document tracking in LibreOffice Writer allow multiple contributors to add, modify, or delete text while clearly showing all revisions in the same file. To enable revision tracking, navigate to Edit, select Changes, and enable the Record option, ensuring that the Show option is also active. When text is inserted, it appears in a distinct color, and hovering over it displays the reviewer's name along with the timestamp of the edit. This name is drawn from the user details entered when LibreOffice was installed. Deleting text does not remove it immediately; instead, it marks the content for deletion and identifies who flagged it. LibreOffice Writer visually differentiates revisions by assigning unique colors to edits made by different reviewers. Hovering over any altered text identifies who performed the modification. Multiple users can thus collaborate, review each other's additions and removals across shared documents, and accept or reject edits before finalizing the document.",
